hi there steve kaufman you know some  while ago i did a video on classroom  learning and  independent learning  and i sort of made them almost it may  have appeared as if i was contrasting  the one with the other  and  certainly i have had some rather un  dynamic and  unsuccessful  language learning experience in  classrooms and i think many of us have  but one should always be careful because  i have met a teacher  a tremendously dynamic teacher who  teaches high school in the united states  in delaware  and uh he i had an interaction with his  class spanish class he's a teacher of  spanish  and i talked to some of his students who  have learned extremely well and who are  very enthusiastic because the is  enthusiastic  and in fact we have developed a program  with them around link which is becomes  in a one of the tools that he uses  uh he's very much  proponent of the crashing approach the  input based learning approach in fact he  organized a conference  at his school where he invited educators  in the area and he had stephen crash and  come  and and present to them  more than once and i also participated  in that discussion as well  and there are other equally enthusiastic  teachers at school on elsewhere  so  i just want to mention this it was  exciting for me to talk first of all to  uh the learners this teachers spanish  learners and then to talk to other  teachers down there and just to see that  sometimes although the you know the  weight the inertia of curricula of  you know everything that is sort of  part of that whole institutionalized  learning  system that we have some of that  can sometimes discourage initiatives but  here's a teacher and others like him who  are doing what they think is best for  their students and have infected their  students with this enthusiasm for  language learning and it was very very  encouraging to see so i'm not naming any  names because i don't have really his  permission to talk about him  but i just want to say that if you have  an enthusiastic teacher and who  understands the importance of of input  and enjoying the language and real  meaningful situations in the language  the classroom can be a wonderful place  to learn  so thank you for listening
 

